title: The Leipzig Congress
subtitle: The Eighth Party Congress meets at the end of January.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: congress_number = 8 and time >= 2
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
var RF = window.RF;
RF.normalize(Q);
Q.mo_passed_news = '';
var d = RF.delegateShares(Q);
Q.leipzig_delegates = RF.delegateHemicycle(d, 150);
Q.leipzig_legend = RF.factionLegend(d);
Q.leipzig_districts = RF.districtsHtml(Q);
!}

= The Eighth Party Congress, Leipzig

The delegates meet in Leipzig from 28 January, a fortnight after the French marched into the Ruhr. They come from the districts, and each district sends mostly its own majority's people.

{!<div class="rf-district-wrap">!}[+ leipzig_districts +]{!</div>!}

{!<div class="rf-delegates">!}[+ leipzig_delegates +]{!<div class="rf-legend">!}[+ leipzig_legend +]{!</div></div>!}

The <span class="f-right">Brandler Right</span> has the majority, and the Zentrale's motions will decide the line. You decide which version of each motion the Zentrale tables. The factions vote by their convictions: the Right will not table what it stands against, and every compromise costs it some patience. <span class="m-radek rf-person col-comintern">Karl Radek</span> is here for the International.

- @wg: Open the debate.

@wg
title: The workers' government
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! window.RF.motionIntro(Q, 'leipzig', 'wg'); !}

= The workers' government

[+ mo_text +]

- @wg_theses
- @wg_amended
- @wg_counter

@wg_theses
title: Table the Zentrale's theses as drafted.
subtitle: <span class="f-right">Right</span> for, <span class="f-left">Left</span> against, <span class="f-minor">Minor currents</span> divided. SPD relations and the party's appeal up; Radek pleased, Zinoviev cool.
choose-if: mo_ok_theses = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Right will not table this: it goes against its core ideas.
on-arrival: {! window.RF.motionVote(Q, 'leipzig', 'wg', 'theses'); !}
go-to: wg_done

@wg_amended
title: Table the theses with the commission's amendments: "a step, not a road".
subtitle: <span class="f-right">Right</span> for, <span class="f-left">Left</span> divided, <span class="f-minor">Minor currents</span> for. A smaller gain with the SPD, a little readiness; Radek and Zinoviev both pleased.
choose-if: mo_ok_amended = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Right will not table this: it goes against its core ideas.
on-arrival: {! window.RF.motionVote(Q, 'leipzig', 'wg', 'amended'); !}
go-to: wg_done

@wg_counter
title: Table the Left's counter-theses.
subtitle: <span class="f-right">Right</span> against, <span class="f-left">Left</span> for, <span class="f-minor">Minor currents</span> divided. Breaks with the SPD; Zinoviev pleased.
choose-if: mo_ok_counter = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Right will not table this: it goes against its core ideas.
on-arrival: {! window.RF.motionVote(Q, 'leipzig', 'wg', 'counter'); !}
go-to: wg_done

@wg_done
new-page: true

= The workers' government

[+ mo_result +]

